The Rainmaster of São Paulo

♫2360978195

The thunder clouds gathered o'er Monaco’s bay,  
When the world first beheld how the red car could play.  
Through the blinding white spray of the downpour and slip,  
The young man from Brazil held the wheel in his grip.  
With a fiery spirit and ice in his veins,  
Ayrton Senna took flight in the heaviest rains.  

He drove on the edge where the mortals would fear,  
Chasing ghosts in the cockpit, year after year.  
Three crowns of the world he would claim for his own,  
In the golden McLaren he built as his throne.  
A mystical warrior who prayed to the sky,  
Who refused to believe that the heroes could die.

His rivalry burned with a furious flame,  
A chess match of speed in a dangerous game.  
But the pride of Brazil was a savior to those  
Who lived in the slums where the poverty rose.  
He gave them his heart, and he gave them his light,  
A flash of pure gold in a desperate night.

